      ":question/id": "7e529998-60b8-53c0-bae5-50351fb55c46",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-72757",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ on $T?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2+(2)(1) & -2+(2)(3) & 1+(2)(2)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
